    "result": "I implemented `order_total` in `solution.py` following `spec.md` and wrote 52 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. Running `python -m pytest -q tests` gives 52 passed.\n\nThe implementation keeps the given signature and `CouponError`, and splits the work into small helpers: subtotal and item validation, coupon checks, discount calculation, and shipping. Shipping is decided on the post-discount amount, is free at 100.00 or more, and is waived only for an empty item list. The final total is quantized to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. The tests cover the boundaries the spec names (expiry day, the minimum-subtotal equality case, the 100% percent cap, the fixed-discount cap, the free-shipping threshold after discount) and the rounding case 0.025 → 0.03.\n\nI did not run coverage, mutation, CRAP or bandit gates, since the only permitted shell command was the test run. I checked coverage by reading the code: every branch in `solution.py` is exercised by at least one test. Mutation strength is unmeasured, though the boundary tests should catch the common operator and constant changes.",
